WEBVTT

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.745
Oh, sir...

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.715
we, um... we're just...

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.615
Yes, I can see that.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.581
What was that all about?

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.956
I'd call it an example

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.393
of indiscreet shipboard
fraternization.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.396
Really?

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.658
Sorry I missed it.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.256
Deck 6.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.836
Thank you for your help, Tom.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.170
Yeah. See you later.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.196
Right.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.747
Here's the cabbage
you asked for.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.840
Is something wrong?

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.744
What's this?

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.223
A spawn beetle.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:01.193
Oh, they cross-pollinate
the Oblissian cabbage.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:05.425
Have you ever seen
such fascinating striations?

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.901
Oh, isn't it beautiful?

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.562
I doubt the Captain
would think so

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.367
if she found it crawling around
in her salad.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.768
There is something wrong.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:18.971
What is it?

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:19.979
No, nothing.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.513
I'm just very busy.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:29.717
So, you're seeing
Tom Paris later.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:30.848
What?

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.949
No, not that I know of.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.459
He said, "See you later."

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.692
You said, "Right."

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.701
Is he helping you
in the airponics bay now?

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.067
He was just helping me
carry these.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:47.163
How thoughtful.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.902
Neelix, this is getting
ridiculous.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.001
You're imagining things
that aren't there.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.103
You're such an innocent!

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.612
I see the way he looks at you.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.117
I used to look at women
that way.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.517
I know what it means.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.920
Janeway to the senior staff.
Please report to the Bridge.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.590
Take care.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.793
Thank you for bringing
the cabbage.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.566
I can handle this from here,
thank you.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.848
We've detected
a strange energy configuration

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:32.909
off the port bow.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.749
Any idea what it is?

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.119
It appears to be some sort
of magnetic disturbance.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.057
We're going to take
a closer look.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.091
You seem a little preoccupied,
Commander.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.895
This morning,
I interrupted a couple

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.595
who were kissing
in the turbolift.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.264
And I've been wondering
if we should establish

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:56.002
a policy regarding...
fraternization.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.476
Well...

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.446
the couple in question
might be urged

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.278
to show a bit more discretion,

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.944
but Starfleet has always
been reluctant

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.351
to regulate
people's personal lives.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.856
Of course, but we're in
a unique situation here.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.552
The development
of intimate relationships

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:16.653
might cause us problems that
wouldn't arise in other ships.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:20.291
I understand
what you're saying, but...

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.927
we're a long way from home.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:26.769
Everyone is lonely,
and all we have is each other.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:30.435
I think, eventually,
people will begin to pair off.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.603
Including you?

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:38.708
As Captain, that's a luxury
I don't have.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:43.984
Besides, I intend for us
to be home before...

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.752
before Mark
gives me up for dead.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.987
We're in visual range,
Captain.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.995
On screen.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:04:00.004
Looks like some type
of energetic vapor.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.573
Magnify.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.102
Space-dwelling life-forms.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.238
Full sensor scan, Mr. Kim.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.248
Their internal

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.113
energy patterns appear
to be consistent

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.640
with discrete organic processes.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.518
Captain, I'd like the chance
to study them at close range.

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.216
So would I, Commander.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.191
But let's not get too close.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.193
We wouldn't want to disturb
their natural behavior.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.195
Half impulse, Mr. Paris.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.890
Take us into bio-scanner range.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.330
Aye, Captain.

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.458
The swarm is not
particularly dense, Captain.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.927
I estimate their number
at fewer than 2,000.

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:11.258
They're really moving.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.264
He's right.

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:13.925
They've accelerated
to a velocity

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:16.729
of approximately
1,000 kilometers per second.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.066
It's possible
we're frightening them.

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:19.366
Keep us within scanner range,

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.839
Lieutenant, but try
to avoid rapid acceleration.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:22.932
Aye, Captain.

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:24.134
Take a look at this.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.178
See the way they
propel themselves?

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:35.083
They seem to flagellate,
almost like protozoa.

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:38.420
Exactly, but they're
achieving incredible speeds...

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.948
over 3,000 kilometers
per second.

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:42.255
Ensign Wildman,

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:44.320
scan the field
for repeating patterns.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.422
Maybe they're capable
of some type of communication.

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:47.523
Aye, Captain.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.364
Their internal anatomy's
also very unusual.

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:52.371
They don't appear to have a
digestive system of any kind,

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.635
but they have an extremely
porous outer covering.

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:55.698
My guess would be

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.301
that they absorb nutrients
directly from space.

00:07:58.344 --> 00:07:59.868
Incredible.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:01.436
A space-dwelling life-form

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.914
capable of metabolizing
inorganic matter.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.178
Particle density

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:06.912
in this part of space
isn't very high.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:09.817
That might explain why they
have to keep moving so fast.

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:12.517
Feeding at 3,000
kilometers per second.

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:15.049
Not exactly leisurely dining,
is it?

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:37.471
Come in.

00:08:44.189 --> 00:08:46.316
For you, sweeting.

00:08:46.357 --> 00:08:48.086
Thank you.

00:08:48.126 --> 00:08:50.651
Hmm... what's the occasion?

00:08:50.695 --> 00:08:52.686
Oh, no occasion.

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:57.259
I... I just wanted to apologize.

00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:59.099
Apologize?

00:08:59.137 --> 00:09:02.072
For the way I acted
in the Mess Hall.

00:09:02.107 --> 00:09:05.338
I-I was jealous.

00:09:05.376 --> 00:09:07.003
I know.

00:09:07.045 --> 00:09:08.910
I just wish you could trust me.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.006
It has nothing to do
with trusting you.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.177
It's him I don't trust.

00:09:14.219 --> 00:09:15.618
I've seen his kind before.

00:09:15.653 --> 00:09:18.349
They're all over the Quadrant,
as a matter of fact.

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:22.917
They prey on naive, sheltered
young women like you.

00:09:22.961 --> 00:09:24.121
What are you looking for?

00:09:24.162 --> 00:09:25.390
A vase.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.055
Don't!

00:09:27.899 --> 00:09:29.423
What's this?

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:31.059
Nothing. Just a snack.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.760
A Terran delicacy.

00:09:33.805 --> 00:09:36.672
Ensign Wildman told me about it.

00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:38.699
Mashed potatoes with butter.

00:09:38.743 --> 00:09:40.506
It's delicious.

00:09:40.545 --> 00:09:42.979
Would you like to try it?

00:09:47.352 --> 00:09:48.717
Ugh. Awful.

00:09:48.753 --> 00:09:50.380
How can you eat it?

00:09:50.421 --> 00:09:52.150
I can't stop eating it.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.953
I've had six bowls.

00:09:54.025 --> 00:09:55.822
And the reason
it tastes so strange...

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:59.296
I put a container
of nitrogenated soil in it.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.524
Dirt?

00:10:00.565 --> 00:10:02.726
You're eating dirt?

00:10:02.767 --> 00:10:03.927
Why?

00:10:03.968 --> 00:10:05.094
I don't know,

00:10:05.136 --> 00:10:06.433
but this morning...

00:10:07.806 --> 00:10:09.774
What?

00:10:09.808 --> 00:10:13.403
You remember the spawn beetles?

00:10:13.444 --> 00:10:15.878
You... you didn't?

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.077
Neelix to Sick Bay.

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:23.087
Prepare to receive
an emergency patient.

00:10:23.121 --> 00:10:24.816
I'm not sick.

00:10:24.856 --> 00:10:27.086
I feel fine.

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:30.993
I just can't... stop eating.

00:10:31.029 --> 00:10:33.156
We are going to get
to the bottom of this.

00:10:33.198 --> 00:10:34.165
Come on.

00:10:34.199 --> 00:10:35.166
No! I'm not going!

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.167
We are going to Sick Bay.

00:10:36.201 --> 00:10:37.259
No!

00:10:37.302 --> 00:10:38.735
I'll call Security
unless you come with me.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.294
Holy...

00:10:40.338 --> 00:10:41.305
Come on.

00:10:41.339 --> 00:10:42.306
Stop it!

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.398
Put me down!

00:10:44.576 --> 00:10:47.136
They're changing course
again, Captain,

00:10:47.178 --> 00:10:49.112
and accelerating.

00:10:49.147 --> 00:10:50.409
Should I follow them?

00:10:50.448 --> 00:10:51.847
I'm concerned
that we're disturbing them.

00:10:51.883 --> 00:10:53.908
Let's drop back a bit,
give them a little more room.

00:10:53.952 --> 00:10:55.442
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:57.121 --> 00:10:59.453
Captain, we're accelerating.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.048
We're getting closer
to the swarm.

00:11:01.092 --> 00:11:02.286
Mr. Paris?

00:11:02.327 --> 00:11:05.160
I'm trying to slow down,
Captain.

00:11:05.196 --> 00:11:08.757
Our velocity doesn't correspond
to impulse reactor output.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.927
We're moving much faster
than we ought to be.

00:11:10.969 --> 00:11:13.130
They seem to be...

00:11:13.171 --> 00:11:14.468
pulling us toward them.

00:11:14.505 --> 00:11:17.201
Sensors indicate
an EM resonance field.

00:11:17.242 --> 00:11:18.732
The creatures
seem to be creating

00:11:18.776 --> 00:11:19.936
their own magnetic wake.

00:11:19.978 --> 00:11:21.411
That is what is pulling
the ship.

00:11:21.446 --> 00:11:23.311
We're getting closer.

00:11:23.348 --> 00:11:24.815
Mr. Paris, reverse thrusters.

00:11:25.817 --> 00:11:27.910
Helm controls aren't responding,
Captain.

00:11:27.952 --> 00:11:30.011
Mr. Tuvok, raise shields.

00:11:31.189 --> 00:11:32.588
Nonfunctional, Captain.

00:11:32.624 --> 00:11:34.023
They're pulling us in.

00:11:47.672 --> 00:11:48.900
Damage report.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:51.272
Life support's functioning
normally, Captain,

00:11:51.309 --> 00:11:53.869
but there's a huge fluctuation
in the EPS grids.

00:11:53.912 --> 00:11:55.743
It's wreaking havoc
with the impulse engines.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.374
Warp drive's still on line.

00:11:58.416 --> 00:11:59.906
One burst,
and we'd be out of here.

00:11:59.951 --> 00:12:02.215
But our exhaust could
seriously harm the creatures.

00:12:02.253 --> 00:12:03.550
Janeway to Torres.

00:12:03.588 --> 00:12:06.113
Do you have any thoughts about
how to get us out of this swarm

00:12:06.157 --> 00:12:07.419
without engaging warp engines?

00:12:07.458 --> 00:12:10.689
We might try something like
a targ scoop.

00:12:10.728 --> 00:12:12.923
Can you enlighten us,
Lieutenant?

00:12:12.964 --> 00:12:15.694
Klingons put them on the front
of ground assault vehicles.

00:12:15.733 --> 00:12:17.792
They emit
a high-frequency tone

00:12:17.835 --> 00:12:20.133
that disperses targ herds
in their path.

00:12:20.171 --> 00:12:21.832
I can modify

00:12:21.873 --> 00:12:24.899
the main deflector to create
an inverted magnetic pulse.

00:12:24.943 --> 00:12:26.934
Project it toward the swarm.

00:12:26.978 --> 00:12:30.937
It might be enough to... nudge
the creatures out of the way.

00:12:30.982 --> 00:12:32.381
Good idea, Lieutenant.

00:12:32.417 --> 00:12:33.907
Proceed.

00:12:33.952 --> 00:12:36.682
You're sure the beetles
weren't poisonous?

00:12:36.721 --> 00:12:38.245
Or the flowers?

00:12:38.289 --> 00:12:41.087
There are no toxins
present in her system.

00:12:41.125 --> 00:12:44.788
Doctor, why is she eating
all these strange things?

00:12:44.829 --> 00:12:45.989
What's wrong with her?

00:12:46.097 --> 00:12:49.498
I am conducting an examination
in order to determine that.

00:12:49.534 --> 00:12:51.627
But don't you have any ideas?

00:12:51.669 --> 00:12:55.833
Her unusual appetite may merely
indicate a nutrient deficiency.

00:12:55.873 --> 00:12:57.170
It is not unusual for humanoids

00:12:57.208 --> 00:12:59.335
to crave foods that are rich
in the very vitamins

00:12:59.377 --> 00:13:01.607
and minerals
that their bodies are lacking.

00:13:01.646 --> 00:13:05.309
You... you can't mean
my body lacks dirt.

00:13:07.685 --> 00:13:10.813
Her body temperature
is elevated 3.9 degrees.

00:13:10.855 --> 00:13:12.379
She's burning up.

00:13:12.423 --> 00:13:13.913
And I'm detecting
elevated levels

00:13:13.958 --> 00:13:16.290
of electrophoretic activity
in her nervous system.

00:13:16.327 --> 00:13:17.885
You have to bring them down.

00:13:17.929 --> 00:13:20.124
There is increased
electrophoretic activity

00:13:20.164 --> 00:13:21.722
in the ship's atmosphere,

00:13:21.766 --> 00:13:24.064
probably created
by the creatures we're studying.

00:13:24.102 --> 00:13:25.467
You mean, there's a connection

00:13:25.503 --> 00:13:27.971
between what's happening to Kes
and those creatures?

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:30.668
You have to do
something about it!

00:13:30.708 --> 00:13:32.471
You are making it impossible
for me to think,

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.410
much less treat my patient.

00:13:34.445 --> 00:13:35.412
You must leave.

00:13:35.446 --> 00:13:37.209
I won't.
Kes needs me.

00:13:37.248 --> 00:13:39.682
Leave now
or I will call Security.

00:13:39.717 --> 00:13:42.811
You can't talk to me that way.

00:13:42.854 --> 00:13:44.151
This is my Sick Bay

00:13:44.188 --> 00:13:45.450
and I will decide
what goes on here.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.650
- But...
- Get out!

00:13:48.359 --> 00:13:49.485
I'll be back.

00:13:49.527 --> 00:13:51.017
Don't worry about a thing.

00:14:07.245 --> 00:14:08.735
Captain, may I speak with you?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.270
It's a matter of some urgency.

00:14:10.314 --> 00:14:11.804
What is it, Neelix?

00:14:11.849 --> 00:14:14.784
I have been thrown
out of Sick Bay.

00:14:17.121 --> 00:14:20.181
And I'm just wondering
if you feel it's appropriate

00:14:20.224 --> 00:14:23.921
for a hologram to banish
a flesh and blood person,

00:14:23.961 --> 00:14:25.690
who should have the right
to be at the bedside

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:27.698
of his loved one,
who is extremely ill.

00:14:27.732 --> 00:14:29.666
Kes is extremely ill?

00:14:30.868 --> 00:14:33.496
The hologram doesn't have a clue
as to what's wrong with her.

00:14:33.538 --> 00:14:35.938
Though it may have something
to do with these creatures.

00:14:35.973 --> 00:14:38.840
But he still won't let me offer
comfort to the woman I love

00:14:38.876 --> 00:14:41.003
at a time when my place
is clearly by her side.

00:14:44.148 --> 00:14:46.776
Just how is Kes being
affected by the swarm?

00:14:46.818 --> 00:14:50.345
That's what I wanted to know,
but before I got any answers,

00:14:50.388 --> 00:14:51.855
I was summarily dismissed.

00:14:51.889 --> 00:14:52.981
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:14:53.024 --> 00:14:54.252
Janeway here.

00:14:54.292 --> 00:14:55.987
Captain, I think
you'd better come down here.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:57.789
There's a bit of a problem.

00:14:57.829 --> 00:14:58.818
I'm on my way.

00:14:58.863 --> 00:15:00.228
Commander, you have the Bridge.

00:15:00.264 --> 00:15:01.424
Notify me immediately

00:15:01.466 --> 00:15:02.592
of any change in our status.

00:15:02.633 --> 00:15:03.759
Aye, Captain.

00:15:05.436 --> 00:15:07.370
I was conducting tests.

00:15:07.405 --> 00:15:09.373
She was none too cooperative,
let me assure you.

00:15:09.407 --> 00:15:10.669
Then suddenly, she screeched

00:15:10.708 --> 00:15:12.767
and shoved me out of the way,
went into my office

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.540
and proceeded to erect
a-a force field at the door.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.979
I can't lower it.

00:15:18.516 --> 00:15:20.381
She's keeping me
out of my own office.

00:15:20.418 --> 00:15:21.942
Sweeting.

00:15:22.987 --> 00:15:24.454
What's wrong?

00:15:24.489 --> 00:15:25.854
Please come out.

00:15:27.258 --> 00:15:29.351
I was able to complete
several tests

00:15:29.393 --> 00:15:31.361
before she became delirious.

00:15:31.395 --> 00:15:32.487
Her fever has increased

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.828
and her pulse and blood pressure
are dangerously high.

00:15:34.866 --> 00:15:37.699
Do you have any idea
what's causing these symptoms?

00:15:37.735 --> 00:15:39.566
I suspect it's
the electrophoretic levels

00:15:39.604 --> 00:15:41.367
being created by the swarm.

00:15:41.405 --> 00:15:43.635
We should leave immediately.

00:15:43.674 --> 00:15:45.904
Unfortunately, that's
not an option at the moment,

00:15:45.943 --> 00:15:47.069
but we're working on it.

00:15:48.346 --> 00:15:49.404
There's one more thing.

00:15:49.447 --> 00:15:52.712
I discovered a strange growth
on her back.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.217
It's unlike
any other tumorous substance

00:15:54.252 --> 00:15:56.243
I've ever seen
or studied before.

00:15:56.287 --> 00:15:59.085
And it was not there
the last time I examined her.

00:16:02.126 --> 00:16:03.957
I'll try to talk to her.

00:16:07.698 --> 00:16:09.757
Kes, please come out.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.768
You can eat anything you want.

00:16:14.372 --> 00:16:15.396
Captain.

00:16:16.474 --> 00:16:17.964
Why don't you let me try?

00:16:23.281 --> 00:16:27.217
Kes, please listen to me.

00:16:27.251 --> 00:16:29.879
We think you're being affected

00:16:29.921 --> 00:16:32.116
by a swarm
of space-dwelling life-forms.

00:16:32.156 --> 00:16:34.522
We're doing everything we can
to get away from them.

00:16:34.559 --> 00:16:37.756
And when we do, you'll probably
start feeling better.

00:16:39.997 --> 00:16:43.330
Are you... saying that's
not what's wrong with you?

00:16:48.772 --> 00:16:52.469
Kes... please, let me come in.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.774
Tell me what it is.

00:16:54.812 --> 00:16:56.643
Maybe I can help.

00:17:17.768 --> 00:17:19.633
Shh.

00:17:20.604 --> 00:17:21.935
Shh.

00:17:21.972 --> 00:17:24.532
It's going to be all right.

00:17:28.846 --> 00:17:31.041
Now...

00:17:31.081 --> 00:17:35.017
tell me what
is happening to you.

00:17:36.787 --> 00:17:38.345
Di-did the Doctor tell you

00:17:38.389 --> 00:17:40.516
he found something
growing on my back?

00:17:40.558 --> 00:17:43.186
Yes, a growth of some kind.

00:17:43.227 --> 00:17:45.821
It's the mitral sac.

00:17:45.863 --> 00:17:48.491
It's where my child would grow.

00:17:49.867 --> 00:17:53.667
I'm going through the elogium...
the time of change...

00:17:53.704 --> 00:17:57.800
when my body prepares
for fertilization.

00:18:01.312 --> 00:18:05.214
Humans go through
the same kind of process.

00:18:05.249 --> 00:18:07.615
It's called puberty.

00:18:07.651 --> 00:18:09.585
But I'm too young.

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.349
Much too young.

00:18:11.388 --> 00:18:16.348
It usually happens between
the ages of four and five.

00:18:16.393 --> 00:18:19.726
I'm-I'm not even two yet.

00:18:19.763 --> 00:18:22.254
Listen to me.

00:18:22.299 --> 00:18:26.133
All your body's metabolic
activity has increased.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:28.400
It's possible
your reproductive processes

00:18:28.439 --> 00:18:30.930
are being accelerated
as a result.

00:18:30.975 --> 00:18:32.704
I'm not ready.

00:18:32.743 --> 00:18:34.768
We're going to get you
through this, Kes.

00:18:34.812 --> 00:18:37.474
The Doctor will monitor
you constantly.

00:18:37.514 --> 00:18:39.812
You don't understand.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.546
The elogium occurs only once.

00:18:42.586 --> 00:18:43.951
If I am ever going
to have a child,

00:18:44.054 --> 00:18:45.453
it has to be now!

00:18:51.095 --> 00:18:52.460
No change, Captain.

00:18:52.496 --> 00:18:54.726
We're still being pulled
along with the swarm.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.730
Heading 121, mark 7.

00:18:58.769 --> 00:19:01.260
Speed now 6,000
kilometers per second.

00:19:01.305 --> 00:19:04.331
All systems are functioning
within normal parameters.

00:19:04.375 --> 00:19:05.342
How is Torres coming

00:19:05.376 --> 00:19:07.241
with the modifications
to the main deflector?

00:19:07.278 --> 00:19:08.506
Her last report estimated

00:19:08.545 --> 00:19:10.103
they'd be finished
in another half hour.

00:19:10.147 --> 00:19:12.012
Let me know
as soon as she's ready.

00:19:12.049 --> 00:19:13.676
Join me, Commander?

00:19:18.222 --> 00:19:19.917
Kes is terribly frightened.

00:19:19.957 --> 00:19:22.187
She's had no time
to prepare for this,

00:19:22.226 --> 00:19:26.686
and the decision has to be made
in the next 40 or 50 hours.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:29.858
She's going to discuss
it with Neelix, but...

00:19:32.036 --> 00:19:34.937
there are so many unknowns.

00:19:35.039 --> 00:19:38.031
There might be risks
in procreating this early.

00:19:38.075 --> 00:19:39.736
And of course
there's no guarantee

00:19:39.777 --> 00:19:41.301
they're genetically compatible,

00:19:41.345 --> 00:19:45.213
or that Neelix has any interest
in becoming a father.

00:19:46.383 --> 00:19:47.941
Seems your concerns

00:19:48.052 --> 00:19:51.385
about fraternization
were... prophetic.

00:19:51.422 --> 00:19:55.688
I wasn't even thinking
about procreation,

00:19:55.726 --> 00:20:00.527
but I suppose it's...
the inevitable outcome.

00:20:02.833 --> 00:20:05.393
We should consider the fact
that it might be necessary

00:20:05.436 --> 00:20:07.063
for the crew to start
having children.

00:20:07.104 --> 00:20:10.403
It might take us
a long time to get home.

00:20:10.441 --> 00:20:13.877
If it does take 75 years,
we're going to need

00:20:13.911 --> 00:20:16.436
a replacement crew
in about half that time.

00:20:18.215 --> 00:20:21.616
Who'd have thought we'd be
considering a generational ship

00:20:21.652 --> 00:20:24.485
when we were ordered
on a three-week mission.

00:20:24.521 --> 00:20:27.957
I know, but it's a problem
we have to face now.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.585
What would that mean
for the children?

00:20:34.031 --> 00:20:36.829
What kind of life
would we be giving them?

00:20:36.867 --> 00:20:38.391
Aboard a starship,

00:20:38.435 --> 00:20:41.996
traveling through a potentially
hostile part of space.

00:20:42.072 --> 00:20:45.906
And are we equipped to provide
for their needs...

00:20:45.943 --> 00:20:48.173
child-care,
educational facilities.

00:20:48.212 --> 00:20:51.511
We'd be building an entire
community on board this ship.

00:20:51.548 --> 00:20:54.142
That's a massive commitment.

00:20:54.184 --> 00:20:56.982
Are you prepared to tell them
they can't have children?

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:59.011
I can't do that.

00:21:02.259 --> 00:21:04.659
And I've made it clear
to Kes that it's her choice

00:21:04.695 --> 00:21:06.959
whether to have a child
or not, but...

00:21:07.064 --> 00:21:08.224
Mmm.

00:21:08.265 --> 00:21:10.825
There aren't
any easy answers here...

00:21:10.868 --> 00:21:13.860
for any of us.

00:21:17.207 --> 00:21:21.268
Are you saying that,
unless you conceive now,

00:21:21.311 --> 00:21:22.972
you'll never be able to?

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:26.447
Yes, and I need you
to help me decide,

00:21:26.483 --> 00:21:28.610
because I would want
you to mate with me.

00:21:32.956 --> 00:21:37.552
I'm... I'm... I'm...
I'm... I'm... I'm...

00:21:37.594 --> 00:21:38.993
honored.

00:21:39.029 --> 00:21:42.658
But are you entirely
certain it would be safe?

00:21:42.699 --> 00:21:43.791
Safe?

00:21:45.469 --> 00:21:47.937
You're so young.

00:21:47.971 --> 00:21:52.806
Is it dangerous for you
to conceive a child at your age?

00:21:52.843 --> 00:21:53.969
I don't know.

00:21:54.011 --> 00:21:57.105
I've never known anyone
as young as I am who had a baby.

00:22:02.286 --> 00:22:06.279
If you never had a child,
would you...

00:22:06.323 --> 00:22:07.449
be terribly unhappy?

00:22:07.491 --> 00:22:08.924
Yes!

00:22:08.959 --> 00:22:10.790
I-I mean...

00:22:10.828 --> 00:22:12.227
I think so.

00:22:14.131 --> 00:22:15.860
I don't know.

00:22:17.968 --> 00:22:20.960
I always assumed
I'd be a mother someday...

00:22:21.038 --> 00:22:24.474
just not so soon.

00:22:26.176 --> 00:22:27.143
What about you?

00:22:27.177 --> 00:22:29.509
Didn't you think
you'd be a father someday?

00:22:29.546 --> 00:22:33.778
Well, to be honest, uh...

00:22:33.817 --> 00:22:36.411
I've never given it
much thought.

00:22:36.453 --> 00:22:42.255
Until now, my life
has been so... itinerant.

00:22:42.292 --> 00:22:45.159
There's no way
I could have provided

00:22:45.195 --> 00:22:47.527
the stability
a child would need.

00:22:47.564 --> 00:22:49.828
But now it's different,
isn't it?

00:22:51.034 --> 00:22:52.433
Well...

00:22:52.469 --> 00:22:54.369
yes.

00:22:54.404 --> 00:22:56.736
But...

00:22:56.773 --> 00:23:00.106
raising a child on a starship...

00:23:00.143 --> 00:23:03.476
that's hardly what I would
call the ideal environment.

00:23:03.514 --> 00:23:06.415
You don't want a child, do you?

00:23:06.450 --> 00:23:08.611
That's not it at all.

00:23:08.652 --> 00:23:12.816
I'm just trying to look
at all sides of the issue.

00:23:14.391 --> 00:23:17.326
Bringing a child
into the world...

00:23:17.361 --> 00:23:19.829
it's a huge responsibility.

00:23:19.863 --> 00:23:23.822
I know you'd want to be sure
we're both up to the task.

00:23:24.968 --> 00:23:27.368
I-I mean, somebody
would have to keep their eye

00:23:27.404 --> 00:23:29.133
on the little guy all the time,

00:23:29.172 --> 00:23:32.073
or he'd be off sticking
his finger into an EM conduit

00:23:32.109 --> 00:23:35.977
or playing
with the plasma injectors.

00:23:36.013 --> 00:23:38.174
That's right...
that's called being a parent.

00:23:41.351 --> 00:23:43.410
What about your medical studies?

00:23:43.453 --> 00:23:45.216
You wouldn't be able
to continue them

00:23:45.255 --> 00:23:46.222
if you had a child.

00:23:46.256 --> 00:23:47.280
Of course I would!

00:23:47.324 --> 00:23:49.315
You're just making excuses.

00:23:49.359 --> 00:23:51.224
All you're thinking about
is yourself...

00:23:51.261 --> 00:23:53.559
how much trouble a child
would be for you.

00:23:53.597 --> 00:23:56.122
Look!

00:23:56.166 --> 00:23:57.497
What's that?

00:23:57.534 --> 00:23:59.729
The ipasaphor.

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:01.931
It makes the mating bond
possible.

00:24:02.005 --> 00:24:03.438
It does?

00:24:03.473 --> 00:24:07.500
If we begin, we must stay bonded
for six days.

00:24:07.544 --> 00:24:09.671
Six days?

00:24:09.713 --> 00:24:11.943
In order to ensure conception.

00:24:12.015 --> 00:24:13.744
And after the ipasaphor appears,

00:24:13.784 --> 00:24:17.948
we only have 50 hours
to begin the process.

00:24:18.055 --> 00:24:20.956
So I need to know your answer.

00:24:21.058 --> 00:24:23.959
Uh, well, uh...

00:24:24.061 --> 00:24:25.358
50 hours.

00:24:25.395 --> 00:24:28.796
That's... good.

00:24:31.602 --> 00:24:32.933
That's good.

00:24:35.806 --> 00:24:37.501
We can sleep on it.

00:24:39.443 --> 00:24:41.035
I'll get back to you.

00:24:59.061 --> 00:25:00.153
Sorry.

00:25:00.195 --> 00:25:02.595
I swear I heard you say
lots of pepper sauce.

00:25:06.335 --> 00:25:08.132
What is the lunch special today?

00:25:09.838 --> 00:25:11.362
Well, actually, I didn't

00:25:11.407 --> 00:25:13.773
get around to making
a lunch special.

00:25:13.809 --> 00:25:16.710
But we have some lovely
gabosti stew left over

00:25:16.745 --> 00:25:17.939
from last night.

00:25:18.013 --> 00:25:20.914
Very well, it will do.

00:25:20.949 --> 00:25:24.680
I've... had quite a run on it
as a matter of fact.

00:25:24.720 --> 00:25:27.518
It seems very popular.

00:25:27.556 --> 00:25:30.957
If it is all you are serving,
that would stand to reason.

00:25:31.026 --> 00:25:33.893
You can have it
with or without pepper sauce.

00:25:33.929 --> 00:25:35.055
Without.

00:25:53.148 --> 00:25:54.775
Oh...

00:26:02.157 --> 00:26:04.853
Mr. Tuvok...

00:26:04.893 --> 00:26:06.861
I was wondering.

00:26:06.895 --> 00:26:09.921
You have children, don't you?

00:26:09.965 --> 00:26:11.455
I have four.

00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:14.060
Four! My!

00:26:14.103 --> 00:26:16.663
That's certainly quite a family.

00:26:16.705 --> 00:26:19.902
Tell me...

00:26:19.942 --> 00:26:23.935
what's it like being a father?

00:26:24.046 --> 00:26:27.948
The question is so broad,
it is difficult to respond.

00:26:28.050 --> 00:26:31.577
Well, I mean, it's a lot
of responsibility, isn't it?

00:26:31.620 --> 00:26:33.815
Watching them.

00:26:33.856 --> 00:26:34.948
Caring for them.

00:26:35.057 --> 00:26:36.547
Keeping them safe.

00:26:36.592 --> 00:26:38.719
Giving them an education.

00:26:38.761 --> 00:26:41.355
That is certainly true.

00:26:41.397 --> 00:26:45.128
Sounds like it's a lot more
trouble than it's worth.

00:26:45.167 --> 00:26:48.967
Mr. Neelix,
I am aware of your situation.

00:26:49.037 --> 00:26:50.766
It appears you are in some doubt

00:26:50.806 --> 00:26:53.070
as to the wisdom
of becoming a parent.

00:26:53.108 --> 00:26:57.169
It's just all happening so fast!

00:26:57.212 --> 00:26:59.077
I don't know what to think.

00:26:59.114 --> 00:27:00.411
I can only tell you

00:27:00.449 --> 00:27:02.917
that if you have considerable
doubts about fatherhood,

00:27:02.985 --> 00:27:05.613
it would not be wise
to enter into the process.

00:27:05.654 --> 00:27:09.055
It is so much more overwhelming
than one expects

00:27:09.091 --> 00:27:11.559
that I believe only
the most committed

00:27:11.593 --> 00:27:13.288
should become parents.

00:27:13.328 --> 00:27:15.262
Ah...

00:27:15.297 --> 00:27:17.231
That's what I thought.

00:27:17.266 --> 00:27:21.635
However, I must point out
that, as illogical as it seems,

00:27:21.670 --> 00:27:24.730
being a father can have
infinite rewards...

00:27:24.773 --> 00:27:27.105
far more
than would seem possible.

00:27:27.142 --> 00:27:30.873
My children occupy a significant
portion of my thoughts,

00:27:30.913 --> 00:27:34.815
now more than ever.

00:27:34.850 --> 00:27:36.044
I have heard it said

00:27:36.084 --> 00:27:40.418
that children can bring a lot
of joy into one's life.

00:27:40.456 --> 00:27:43.653
I experience
neither joy nor sorrow,

00:27:43.692 --> 00:27:45.990
but I do believe it is possible.

00:27:48.063 --> 00:27:50.088
Now that I think about it,

00:27:50.132 --> 00:27:53.158
it might be fun
to have a little guy around.

00:27:53.202 --> 00:27:56.865
And we could do a lot together.

00:27:56.905 --> 00:28:00.841
I've got quite a bit
I could teach a boy, you know...

00:28:00.876 --> 00:28:04.505
survival methods,

00:28:04.546 --> 00:28:06.912
piloting skills,

00:28:07.015 --> 00:28:09.108
romantic techniques.

00:28:11.119 --> 00:28:12.450
If you say so.

00:28:12.488 --> 00:28:14.922
But I must point out
that there is an equal chance

00:28:15.023 --> 00:28:16.786
that you would have a daughter.

00:28:16.825 --> 00:28:18.850
A daughter?

00:28:18.894 --> 00:28:21.727
I don't have anything
to teach a daughter.

00:28:21.763 --> 00:28:25.130
Why would it be any different
from what you would teach a son?

00:28:26.134 --> 00:28:28.034
It just would.

00:28:28.070 --> 00:28:30.630
She'd learn more
from her mother.

00:28:30.672 --> 00:28:33.903
I have three sons
and one daughter.

00:28:33.942 --> 00:28:35.705
I can assure you, she benefits

00:28:35.744 --> 00:28:37.939
as much from my presence
and guidance

00:28:38.046 --> 00:28:39.411
as my sons do.

00:28:39.448 --> 00:28:41.780
It is unfortunate

00:28:41.817 --> 00:28:44.684
that I must be so far removed
from all of them now.

00:28:47.623 --> 00:28:49.682
I understand.

00:28:49.725 --> 00:28:52.387
We'll get there, Mr. Vulcan.

00:28:52.427 --> 00:28:54.258
I'm sure of it.

00:28:56.665 --> 00:28:58.565
Thank you.

00:28:58.600 --> 00:29:00.966
You've given me a lot
to think about.

00:29:08.010 --> 00:29:09.102
We're ready to generate

00:29:09.144 --> 00:29:10.406
the inverted
magnetic pulse, Captain.

00:29:10.445 --> 00:29:12.003
Proceed.

00:29:13.849 --> 00:29:15.578
Initiating the field.

00:29:19.154 --> 00:29:20.781
It's working.

00:29:20.822 --> 00:29:22.756
Are the creatures all right,
Commander?

00:29:22.791 --> 00:29:24.918
Yes, Captain,
they seem to be fine.

00:29:24.960 --> 00:29:26.757
Let's try to keep it that way.

00:29:26.795 --> 00:29:28.262
Thrusters at 200 kph,
Mr. Paris.

00:29:28.297 --> 00:29:29.321
Ease us out of here.

00:29:29.364 --> 00:29:30.524
Aye, Captain.

00:29:36.238 --> 00:29:37.205
What are they doing?

00:29:37.239 --> 00:29:39.537
Hard to know
what's prompting that behavior.

00:29:39.575 --> 00:29:41.304
Maybe they think
we're making a hostile move.

00:29:42.377 --> 00:29:43.537
Report.

00:29:43.579 --> 00:29:46.241
I'm reading a massive energy
drain in all ship systems.

00:29:46.281 --> 00:29:47.771
Impulse engines
are losing power.

00:29:47.816 --> 00:29:49.841
Captain,
some of the life-forms

00:29:49.885 --> 00:29:51.443
have attached themselves
to the warp nacelles.

00:29:51.486 --> 00:29:54.284
Guidance, navigational and
tactical systems are failing.

00:29:54.323 --> 00:29:56.086
How soon will we clear
the swarm, Lieutenant?

00:29:56.124 --> 00:29:57.887
In a few seconds.
We're almost out.

00:29:57.926 --> 00:30:01.589
Captain, I am detecting
a substantial magnetic mass

00:30:01.630 --> 00:30:03.655
moving rapidly
toward the port bow.

00:30:16.578 --> 00:30:19.308
It's physiologically similar
to the smaller creatures,

00:30:19.348 --> 00:30:20.713
just a lot bigger.

00:30:20.749 --> 00:30:22.876
Perhaps it is the parent.

00:30:22.918 --> 00:30:24.613
Or it could be
a difference in gender.

00:30:24.653 --> 00:30:27.884
It's hard to say
without further observation.

00:30:27.923 --> 00:30:28.981
With all due respect, Captain,

00:30:29.057 --> 00:30:30.718
haven't we done
enough observing?

00:30:30.759 --> 00:30:33.819
These creatures have attacked
the ship's key systems.

00:30:33.862 --> 00:30:36.387
For all we know, they were
setting us up for an attack.

00:30:36.431 --> 00:30:37.420
It's possible.

00:30:37.466 --> 00:30:39.195
Mr. Paris, let's keep moving.

00:30:39.234 --> 00:30:41.361
If we can put some distance
between us and the swarm,

00:30:41.403 --> 00:30:42.495
maybe the ones on our nacelles

00:30:42.537 --> 00:30:44.869
will drop off
and rejoin their friends.

00:30:44.906 --> 00:30:47.704
Aye, Captain.
200 kph.

00:30:53.749 --> 00:30:55.979
The larger creature
is moving with us.

00:30:57.953 --> 00:30:58.920
Now what?

00:30:58.954 --> 00:31:00.114
The creature has emitted

00:31:00.155 --> 00:31:03.056
an electrically charged
plasma stream.

00:31:03.091 --> 00:31:05.059
All stop.
Damage report.

00:31:06.294 --> 00:31:07.784
No significant damage, Captain.

00:31:07.829 --> 00:31:08.796
Shields are holding.

00:31:08.830 --> 00:31:11.128
A plasma blast
is a hostile move.

00:31:11.166 --> 00:31:13.157
Shouldn't we be thinking
about responding?

00:31:14.369 --> 00:31:16.803
If the creature threatens
serious damage to the ship,

00:31:16.838 --> 00:31:18.465
I'll consider it an enemy.

00:31:18.507 --> 00:31:19.974
Until then,
they're all to be treated

00:31:20.008 --> 00:31:21.976
as indigenous life-forms
behaving normally

00:31:22.044 --> 00:31:23.238
in their natural habitat.

00:31:23.278 --> 00:31:25.109
We're the intruders here.

00:31:25.147 --> 00:31:27.308
Captain, look at this.

00:31:30.018 --> 00:31:31.246
They're attaching themselves

00:31:31.286 --> 00:31:33.811
to the large creature
the same way they did to us.

00:31:33.855 --> 00:31:35.584
And I think I know why.

00:31:35.624 --> 00:31:36.989
That plasma stream it ejected

00:31:37.059 --> 00:31:39.960
has almost the same subspace
signature as our warp nacelles.

00:31:41.196 --> 00:31:42.561
Then the smaller creatures
are attracted

00:31:42.597 --> 00:31:43.996
to our subspace emissions.

00:31:44.066 --> 00:31:45.328
Perhaps in the same way

00:31:45.367 --> 00:31:47.597
some species are attracted
to pheromones.

00:31:47.636 --> 00:31:49.069
Pheromones?

00:31:50.439 --> 00:31:52.839
You think
it's a sexual attraction?

00:31:52.874 --> 00:31:55.342
Color change
and provocative movement

00:31:55.377 --> 00:31:58.437
are frequently associated
with mating rituals.

00:31:58.480 --> 00:32:01.938
Then... these guys think
we're one of them?

00:32:02.017 --> 00:32:02.949
Well, their behavior toward us

00:32:03.051 --> 00:32:04.575
and the large creature
is similar.

00:32:04.619 --> 00:32:08.146
It's possible they've mistaken
us for a potential mate.

00:32:12.761 --> 00:32:13.728
Yes?

00:32:13.762 --> 00:32:16.322
Well, order the diapers.

00:32:16.364 --> 00:32:18.059
We're about to become parents.

00:32:18.100 --> 00:32:21.228
You mean,
you want to mate with me?

00:32:21.269 --> 00:32:23.203
More than anything.

00:32:23.238 --> 00:32:24.569
But you were making excuses.

00:32:24.606 --> 00:32:26.540
I didn't think
you wanted to be a father.

00:32:26.575 --> 00:32:28.975
I just hadn't
thought it through.

00:32:29.010 --> 00:32:32.343
Now that I have, I swear to you
I want to do this.

00:32:32.380 --> 00:32:36.077
And I'll be the best
possible father to our child.

00:32:40.122 --> 00:32:42.089
I know you will.

00:32:42.222 --> 00:32:43.917
So...

00:32:43.957 --> 00:32:46.983
what comes next?

00:32:47.027 --> 00:32:49.086
Before we begin
the mating process,

00:32:49.129 --> 00:32:50.824
I have to go through
a certain ritual

00:32:50.864 --> 00:32:52.422
called the rolisisin.

00:32:52.466 --> 00:32:55.196
What does that involve?

00:32:55.235 --> 00:32:57.965
One of my parents
has to massage my feet

00:32:58.004 --> 00:32:59.995
until my tongue begins to swell.

00:33:03.777 --> 00:33:06.712
Uh, where do you plan
to find a parent?

00:33:06.746 --> 00:33:08.611
If Captain Janeway weren't
so busy I'd ask her,

00:33:08.648 --> 00:33:10.115
but I'm sure
the Doctor would do it.

00:33:10.150 --> 00:33:11.515
Will that work?

00:33:11.551 --> 00:33:14.247
Since he's not a real person?

00:33:14.287 --> 00:33:16.448
The Doctor is very real to me.

00:33:16.490 --> 00:33:20.483
I don't know how I feel
about him massaging your feet.

00:33:20.527 --> 00:33:22.427
It's a ritual.
Someone has to do it.

00:33:22.462 --> 00:33:25.124
Okay. Okay, fine.

00:33:25.165 --> 00:33:27.633
How long will that take?

00:33:28.635 --> 00:33:29.966
About an hour.

00:33:32.005 --> 00:33:33.131
Then I'll be back.

00:33:51.758 --> 00:33:54.318
Fascinating.

00:33:54.361 --> 00:33:55.851
The stimulation
to the sympathetic nerves

00:33:55.896 --> 00:33:57.830
must set off
a hormonal reaction,

00:33:57.864 --> 00:33:59.559
which activates
glandular activity

00:33:59.599 --> 00:34:01.260
in the tissues of the tongue.

00:34:01.301 --> 00:34:03.235
I've never seen
this response before.

00:34:03.270 --> 00:34:05.329
Although in a species
known as the Gree,

00:34:05.372 --> 00:34:07.431
stimulating follicles
on the proboscis

00:34:07.474 --> 00:34:09.567
results in a swelling
of the auricular canal.

00:34:09.609 --> 00:34:10.633
Doctor?

00:34:10.677 --> 00:34:12.201
Yes?

00:34:12.245 --> 00:34:14.873
Am I doing the right thing?

00:34:14.915 --> 00:34:16.883
You'll have to tell me.

00:34:16.917 --> 00:34:19.511
I know nothing of this ritual.

00:34:19.553 --> 00:34:21.111
No, I mean, am I doing
the right thing

00:34:21.154 --> 00:34:22.416
by conceiving a child?

00:34:24.558 --> 00:34:25.820
If I were at home now,

00:34:25.859 --> 00:34:29.818
my father would be performing
the rolisisin with me.

00:34:32.499 --> 00:34:34.228
It's the time
when parent and child

00:34:34.267 --> 00:34:36.167
move into a new kind
of relationship.

00:34:36.203 --> 00:34:38.535
As the child has her own child,

00:34:38.572 --> 00:34:42.508
the parent must acknowledge
her true adulthood.

00:34:42.542 --> 00:34:44.703
I see.

00:34:44.744 --> 00:34:47.838
My father and I were very close.

00:34:47.881 --> 00:34:49.542
He was such a wise man.

00:34:49.583 --> 00:34:51.073
I miss him.

00:34:51.117 --> 00:34:54.143
Sometimes, I think I hear
his voice in my head.

00:34:54.187 --> 00:34:55.984
It's almost
as though he were here

00:34:56.089 --> 00:34:57.181
helping to guide me.

00:35:00.227 --> 00:35:01.922
I'm sorry.

00:35:01.962 --> 00:35:06.592
I must be feeling lonely
for home.

00:35:06.633 --> 00:35:10.660
It's probably a result
of the elogium...

00:35:13.240 --> 00:35:17.472
but I really would appreciate
your advice.

00:35:17.510 --> 00:35:19.501
Your help.

00:35:22.015 --> 00:35:24.279
I need someone's guidance.

00:35:27.153 --> 00:35:29.644
I can discuss
delivery methods...

00:35:29.689 --> 00:35:33.523
or pediatric situations.

00:35:33.560 --> 00:35:36.461
I'm afraid I don't have
much perspective to offer

00:35:36.496 --> 00:35:38.623
about becoming a parent.

00:35:40.200 --> 00:35:42.725
Neither do I.

00:35:42.769 --> 00:35:46.933
As long as Neelix
was opposed to the idea,

00:35:46.973 --> 00:35:48.235
trying to get out of it,

00:35:48.275 --> 00:35:50.641
I was certain that I wanted
to have a child,

00:35:50.677 --> 00:35:52.838
but when he said
that he wanted one, too,

00:35:52.879 --> 00:35:54.938
suddenly, I was very frightened.

00:35:59.586 --> 00:36:04.046
Perhaps a statistical survey
will offer a context.

00:36:04.090 --> 00:36:07.253
Among the Breen,
pregnancy at a young age

00:36:07.294 --> 00:36:08.818
is a common event.

00:36:08.862 --> 00:36:10.056
The Breen, of course,

00:36:10.096 --> 00:36:12.360
is one of the most warlike
of species.

00:36:12.399 --> 00:36:14.230
And then there are the Scathos.

00:36:14.267 --> 00:36:16.064
Any woman who conceives a child

00:36:16.102 --> 00:36:19.162
before her fourth decade
is summarily executed.

00:36:19.205 --> 00:36:21.036
Maybe I just felt
I should have a child

00:36:21.074 --> 00:36:22.098
because I could.

00:36:22.142 --> 00:36:25.600
There is a powerful
biological drive,

00:36:25.645 --> 00:36:28.773
at times, almost impossible
to resist.

00:36:28.815 --> 00:36:32.444
Species are driven by these
urges in order to survive.

00:36:32.485 --> 00:36:34.419
But isn't that
why we have minds...

00:36:34.454 --> 00:36:40.393
to look beyond biological urges,
to consider their consequences?

00:36:40.427 --> 00:36:43.419
If I'm going to ask myself
to look at those consequences,

00:36:43.463 --> 00:36:45.931
then I have to ask myself
some questions.

00:36:45.965 --> 00:36:49.526
Am I really ready
to have a child?

00:36:51.871 --> 00:36:53.361
Am I prepared to give that child

00:36:53.406 --> 00:36:56.739
the attention and devotion
it deserves?

00:36:56.776 --> 00:37:01.179
Am I capable of taking on
such a huge responsibility?

00:37:01.214 --> 00:37:03.239
Oh, there's so much
I haven't done.

00:37:03.283 --> 00:37:05.911
There's so much
I want to study and learn.

00:37:06.019 --> 00:37:08.579
I'm not sure
I'm finished growing.

00:37:08.621 --> 00:37:10.680
How could I help a child grow?

00:37:18.231 --> 00:37:19.391
If the smaller creatures

00:37:19.432 --> 00:37:21.662
are sexually attracted
to our subspace emissions,

00:37:21.701 --> 00:37:24.033
then the large one
may perceive us as a rival.

00:37:24.070 --> 00:37:25.731
That plasma burst it sent out

00:37:25.772 --> 00:37:27.672
might have been
aggressive posturing.

00:37:27.707 --> 00:37:30.369
Then you'd think it would be
happy to see us leave.

00:37:30.410 --> 00:37:32.071
Lieutenant, is there
any way we could generate

00:37:32.112 --> 00:37:33.079
a short burst of impulse?

00:37:33.113 --> 00:37:34.546
Enough to get us away
from this swarm?

00:37:34.581 --> 00:37:35.639
I could try

00:37:35.682 --> 00:37:37.707
releasing power from the
impulse capacitance cells

00:37:37.751 --> 00:37:39.343
straight into the driver coils.

00:37:39.386 --> 00:37:40.410
Do it.

00:37:40.453 --> 00:37:42.182
All right.

00:37:42.222 --> 00:37:45.248
I've accessed
the capacitance cells.

00:37:45.291 --> 00:37:48.658
I think I can give you enough
for a short burst of impulse.

00:37:48.695 --> 00:37:49.957
We've got one shot, Captain.

00:37:50.063 --> 00:37:51.360
You heard her, Mr. Paris.

00:37:51.398 --> 00:37:52.660
Make the best of it.

00:37:52.699 --> 00:37:53.825
Aye, Captain.

00:37:53.867 --> 00:37:55.835
Initiating impulse burst...

00:37:55.869 --> 00:37:57.598
now.

00:37:58.671 --> 00:38:00.468
Captain,
the creature is reacting.

00:38:00.507 --> 00:38:03.237
It is approaching rapidly
on a collision course.

00:38:03.276 --> 00:38:04.903
Evasive maneuvers, Lieutenant.

00:38:04.944 --> 00:38:06.275
We don't have the power
for that.

00:38:06.312 --> 00:38:08.303
The creature is accelerating.

00:38:08.348 --> 00:38:10.077
I'm losing power.
Can't shake him.

00:38:10.116 --> 00:38:11.674
All hands brace for impact.

00:38:28.168 --> 00:38:30.602
Structural integrity
down to 86 percent.

00:38:30.637 --> 00:38:31.626
I am beginning to share

00:38:31.671 --> 00:38:33.138
Lieutenant Torres' views,
Captain.

00:38:33.173 --> 00:38:34.868
Retaliation
may become necessary.

00:38:34.908 --> 00:38:38.105
It's not my intention
to harm the creature.

00:38:38.144 --> 00:38:41.272
The feeling
definitely isn't mutual.

00:38:41.314 --> 00:38:42.781
Mr. Tuvok,
launch a class- 4 probe.

00:38:42.816 --> 00:38:44.511
Maybe that will distract
the creature long enough

00:38:44.551 --> 00:38:45.518
for us to get away.

00:38:45.552 --> 00:38:46.814
Aye, Captain.

00:38:46.853 --> 00:38:48.343
Probe launched.

00:38:49.823 --> 00:38:51.450
Another plasma burst.

00:38:51.491 --> 00:38:52.890
Shields are down to 64 percent.

00:38:52.926 --> 00:38:54.951
Looks like the probe
just made him angry.

00:38:55.028 --> 00:38:56.859
This is an aggressive life-form,
Captain.

00:38:56.896 --> 00:38:59.592
He's only going to respond
to an aggressive stance from us.

00:38:59.632 --> 00:39:01.657
Treating the creature
as it is treating us

00:39:01.701 --> 00:39:03.566
might be
an appropriate response.

00:39:03.603 --> 00:39:05.070
We ram him.

00:39:05.104 --> 00:39:06.401
Precisely.

00:39:06.439 --> 00:39:08.430
It's probably
the response he expects.

00:39:09.943 --> 00:39:12.207
Captain,
shields are at 47 percent.

00:39:12.245 --> 00:39:14.645
Any more of this and the hull
will start to buckle.

00:39:14.681 --> 00:39:16.876
Mr. Paris, use
maneuvering thrusters.

00:39:16.916 --> 00:39:18.281
Set a course
toward the creature.

00:39:18.318 --> 00:39:20.149
Give him a bump
to get his attention.

00:39:20.186 --> 00:39:22.313
Aye, Captain.
Engaging thrusters.

00:39:28.361 --> 00:39:30.386
The creature is not retreating,
Captain.

00:39:32.065 --> 00:39:34.590
He's just hitting us
back harder.

00:39:34.634 --> 00:39:35.931
Let's try this.

00:39:36.035 --> 00:39:37.559
Detonate a field
of photon charges

00:39:37.604 --> 00:39:39.367
between Voyager
and the creature.

00:39:39.405 --> 00:39:40.372
Maybe the shock wave

00:39:40.406 --> 00:39:41.805
will let him know
we mean business.

00:39:41.841 --> 00:39:43.035
Captain, if I may.

00:39:43.076 --> 00:39:45.169
Maybe we're going
about this backwards.

00:39:45.211 --> 00:39:46.576
Yes, Commander?

00:39:46.613 --> 00:39:48.240
Every aggressive move we make

00:39:48.281 --> 00:39:51.045
results in a more aggressive
move by the creature.

00:39:51.084 --> 00:39:52.915
If we're not prepared
to use extreme force

00:39:52.952 --> 00:39:55.284
to destroy him, we need
to rethink our actions.

00:39:55.321 --> 00:39:56.288
I'm listening.

00:39:56.322 --> 00:39:57.880
If we're right that the creature

00:39:57.924 --> 00:39:59.755
is responding to us
as a sexual rival,

00:39:59.792 --> 00:40:01.953
we might try behaving
in a submissive way.

00:40:02.061 --> 00:40:03.494
That may appease him.

00:40:03.530 --> 00:40:04.963
We'd be acknowledging
that he's dominant

00:40:04.998 --> 00:40:06.397
and that we're no match for him.

00:40:06.432 --> 00:40:07.399
How do we do that?

00:40:07.433 --> 00:40:08.695
We tried to move away slowly.

00:40:08.735 --> 00:40:09.895
He wouldn't let us leave.

00:40:09.936 --> 00:40:11.665
Maybe we need to mimic
the behavior

00:40:11.704 --> 00:40:12.966
of the smaller creatures.

00:40:13.039 --> 00:40:15.439
We saw them rolling over
and changing color.

00:40:15.475 --> 00:40:18.137
If we vent plasma residue,

00:40:18.177 --> 00:40:19.838
that might make us look blue.

00:40:19.879 --> 00:40:22.143
Mr. Paris,
do we have enough power

00:40:22.181 --> 00:40:24.172
to take Voyager into a roll?

00:40:24.217 --> 00:40:25.707
I think so.

00:40:25.752 --> 00:40:28.687
All right.
Let's give this a try.

00:40:28.721 --> 00:40:31.155
Mr. Kim, start venting
plasma residue.

00:40:31.190 --> 00:40:34.421
Mr. Paris, roll the ship.

00:40:35.762 --> 00:40:37.889
Full power to inertial dampers.

00:40:49.975 --> 00:40:51.840
He's not responding at all.

00:40:51.877 --> 00:40:52.901
It's not working.

00:40:52.945 --> 00:40:54.003
Wait a minute, Captain.

00:40:54.046 --> 00:40:55.206
What is it?

00:40:55.247 --> 00:40:56.646
One of the small creatures

00:40:56.682 --> 00:40:58.980
is detaching
from the starboard nacelle.

00:40:59.017 --> 00:41:00.848
And another one.

00:41:00.886 --> 00:41:02.717
They're all letting go.

00:41:04.890 --> 00:41:07.552
It appears we have lost
our sex appeal, Captain.

00:41:09.194 --> 00:41:10.786
Good piloting, Lieutenant.

00:41:10.829 --> 00:41:13.923
Now, let's see if we can move
away without any interference.

00:41:13.966 --> 00:41:15.831
I can give you
enough thruster power

00:41:15.868 --> 00:41:18.359
to sustain a speed
of 100 kph.

00:41:18.403 --> 00:41:19.961
Acknowledged.

00:41:20.005 --> 00:41:22.599
Good work, Commander.

00:41:22.641 --> 00:41:23.665
In the future,

00:41:23.709 --> 00:41:25.472
if I have any questions
about mating behavior,

00:41:25.511 --> 00:41:27.172
I'll know where to go.

00:41:57.943 --> 00:41:59.467
Can I help?

00:41:59.511 --> 00:42:01.604
No.

00:42:01.647 --> 00:42:03.308
Thanks.

00:42:04.850 --> 00:42:06.784
Is something wrong?

00:42:06.818 --> 00:42:09.116
No, no, nothing.

00:42:10.155 --> 00:42:11.588
You've been very quiet

00:42:11.623 --> 00:42:13.955
ever since I decided
not to conceive.

00:42:14.059 --> 00:42:17.187
It was your choice.

00:42:17.229 --> 00:42:19.322
I respect that.

00:42:19.364 --> 00:42:22.094
Neelix...

00:42:22.134 --> 00:42:24.102
I think you're disappointed.

00:42:27.706 --> 00:42:30.368
I think...

00:42:30.409 --> 00:42:33.845
once I decided
to become a father,

00:42:33.879 --> 00:42:37.781
I was looking forward to it.

00:42:37.816 --> 00:42:39.784
But I'll get over it.

00:42:39.818 --> 00:42:42.582
Maybe you won't have
to get over it.

00:42:42.621 --> 00:42:44.680
Just wait a little longer.

00:42:44.723 --> 00:42:46.748
But I thought...

00:42:46.792 --> 00:42:48.623
this was the only time.

00:42:48.660 --> 00:42:50.651
The Doctor believes
the elogium was false,

00:42:50.696 --> 00:42:54.427
brought on by
the electrophoretic field

00:42:54.466 --> 00:42:57.833
that those life-forms created.

00:42:57.869 --> 00:42:59.962
So there's a possibility
that I might be able

00:43:00.005 --> 00:43:02.439
to go through it again
at the right age.

00:43:02.474 --> 00:43:05.773
You mean, we might still
be able to have a daughter?

00:43:05.811 --> 00:43:06.778
Or a son.

00:43:06.812 --> 00:43:07.744
No.

00:43:07.779 --> 00:43:08.768
I've thought about it.

00:43:08.814 --> 00:43:11.044
A daughter, definitely...

00:43:11.083 --> 00:43:13.881
one who looks just like you.

00:43:24.997 --> 00:43:29.127
Captain's Log, Stardate 48921.3.

00:43:29.167 --> 00:43:30.259
I continue to wonder

00:43:30.302 --> 00:43:32.634
about the issue of procreation
aboard the ship.

00:43:32.671 --> 00:43:34.366
Certainly, it's wrong
to interfere

00:43:34.406 --> 00:43:36.966
with the private lives
and decisions of the crew.

00:43:37.009 --> 00:43:39.102
Yet I remain concerned
about the environment

00:43:39.144 --> 00:43:41.738
we could provide
for any child born here.

00:43:47.786 --> 00:43:48.775
Come in.

00:43:50.088 --> 00:43:50.986
Yes, Ensign.

00:43:51.089 --> 00:43:52.556
What can I do for you?

00:43:52.591 --> 00:43:54.616
I'm sorry
to disturb you, Captain,

00:43:54.660 --> 00:43:56.457
but I thought...

00:43:56.495 --> 00:44:01.797
I thought I should inform you
of my physical condition.

00:44:02.868 --> 00:44:04.699
Your physical condition?

00:44:06.271 --> 00:44:08.705
Well, we'd been trying
for months.

00:44:08.740 --> 00:44:12.073
I wasn't even sure
until a few days ago.

00:44:12.110 --> 00:44:14.874
My husband is still
at Deep Space 9.

00:44:14.913 --> 00:44:16.437
He doesn't even know.

00:44:16.481 --> 00:44:19.041
We were only supposed to be out
two or three weeks.

00:44:19.084 --> 00:44:21.314
Wildman...

00:44:21.353 --> 00:44:23.116
are you pregnant?

00:44:29.027 --> 00:44:31.689
I know this isn't the best place
to have a baby, but...

00:44:33.231 --> 00:44:35.859
it's all I have left...

00:44:35.901 --> 00:44:37.732
of my husband.

00:44:40.072 --> 00:44:41.972
Well...

00:44:42.074 --> 00:44:44.804
congratulations, Ensign.
